= Body Ritual among the Nacirema / 纳西雷马人的身体仪式

#html.p(id: "en-S001")[#text("The anthropologist has become so familiar with the diversity of ways in which different people behave in similar situations that he is not apt to be surprised by even the most exotic customs. In fact, if all of the logically possible combinations of behavior have not been found somewhere in the world, he is apt to suspect that they must be present in some yet undescribed tribe. The point has, in fact, been expressed with respect to clan organization by Murdock.")]

#zh(id: "S001")[#text("人类学家已经十分熟悉不同民族在相似情境下表现出的种种不同举止，因此，即使面对最奇异的习俗，也不大容易吃惊。事实上，如果世界上还没有发现所有逻辑上可能的行为组合，他反倒会怀疑：这些组合一定存在于某个尚未被描述的部落中。默多克在谈论氏族组织时，确实表达过这一点。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S002")[#text("In this light, the magical beliefs and practices of the Nacirema present such unusual aspects that it seems desirable to describe them as an example of the extremes to which human behavior can go.")]

#zh(id: "S002")[#text("从这个角度看，纳西雷马人的巫术信仰与实践呈现出一些极不寻常的特点，似乎值得加以描述，作为人类行为能够走到何等极端的例子。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S003")[#text("Professor Linton first brought the ritual of the Nacirema to the attention of anthropologists twenty years ago, but the culture of this people is still very poorly understood. They are a North American group living in the territory between the Canadian Cree, the Yaqui and Tarahumare of Mexico, and the Carib and Arawak of the Antilles. Little is known of their origin, although tradition states that they came from the east.")]

#zh(id: "S003")[#text("二十年前，林顿教授首先把纳西雷马人的仪式介绍给人类学家，但这个民族的文化至今仍很少为人所知。他们是一个北美族群，居住在加拿大克里人、墨西哥雅基人与塔拉乌马拉人，以及安的列斯群岛的加勒比人与阿拉瓦克人之间的地域。人们对他们的起源知道得很少，尽管传说称他们来自东方。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S004")[#text("According to Nacirema mythology, their nation was originated by a culture hero, Notgnihsaw, who is otherwise known for two great feats of strength—the throwing of a piece of wampum across the river Pa-To-Mac and the chopping down of a cherry tree in which the Spirit of Truth resided.")]

#zh(id: "S004")[#text("根据纳西雷马人的神话，他们的民族由一位文化英雄 Notgnihsaw 创立。他另外还以两项力量壮举闻名：把一块贝壳串珠抛过 Pa-To-Mac 河，以及砍倒一棵真理之灵栖居其中的樱桃树。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S005")[#text("Nacirema culture is characterized by a highly developed market economy which has evolved in a rich natural habitat. While much of the people's time is devoted to economic pursuits, a large part of the fruits of these labors and a considerable portion of the day are spent in ritual activity. The focus of this activity is the human body, the appearance and health of which loom as a dominant concern in the ethos of the people.")]

#zh(id: "S005")[#text("纳西雷马文化的特点，是在自然资源丰富的环境中发展出高度发达的市场经济。人们的大部分时间虽用于经济活动，但劳动成果中的很大一部分，以及一天中相当多的时间，都花在仪式活动上。这些活动的焦点是人的身体；身体的外观与健康，在这个民族的精神气质中占据主导地位。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S006")[#text("While such a concern is certainly not unusual, its ceremonial aspects and associated philosophy are unique.")]

#zh(id: "S006")[#text("这种关注当然并不罕见，但与之相伴的仪式形式和哲学观念却独具特色。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S007")[#text("The fundamental belief underlying the whole system appears to be that the human body is ugly and that its natural tendency is to debility and disease. Incarcerated in such a body, man's only hope is to avert these characteristics through the use of ritual and ceremony. Every household has one or more shrines devoted to this purpose.")]

#zh(id: "S007")[#text("支撑整个体系的基本信念，似乎是人的身体丑陋，而且天然会走向衰弱与疾病。囚禁在这种身体中，人的唯一希望，就是通过仪式与典礼来避免这些特性。每个家庭都有一个或多个专门用于此目的的圣所。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S008")[#text("The more powerful individuals in the society have several shrines in their houses and, in fact, the opulence of a house is often referred to in terms of the number of such ritual centers it possesses. Most houses are of wattle and daub construction, but the shrine rooms of the more wealthy are walled with stone. Poorer families imitate the rich by applying pottery plaques to their shrine walls.")]

#zh(id: "S008")[#text("社会中更有权势的人，在家中设有几个圣所；事实上，一座房屋的豪华程度，常常以其拥有的这种仪式中心的数量来衡量。大多数房屋用枝条编成骨架，再涂上泥土建成，但富人家中的圣所房间，墙面是石头的。较贫穷的家庭模仿富人，在圣所墙上贴上陶片。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S009")[#text("While each family has at least one such shrine, the rituals associated with it are not family ceremonies but are private and secret. The rites are normally only discussed with children, and then only during the period when they are being initiated into these mysteries. I was able, however, to establish sufficient rapport with the natives to examine these shrines and to have the rituals described to me.")]

#zh(id: "S009")[#text("虽然每个家庭至少都有这样一个圣所，但相关仪式并不是家庭典礼，而是私密、秘密的活动。通常，人们只向孩子谈论这些仪式，而且仅在孩子被引入这些奥秘的阶段才谈。不过，我设法与当地人建立了足够的信任关系，得以察看这些圣所，并听他们描述仪式。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S010")[#text("The focal point of the shrine is a box or chest which is built into the wall. In this chest are kept the many charms and magical potions without which no native believes he could live. These preparations are secured from a variety of specialized practitioners. The most powerful of these are the medicine men, whose assistance must be rewarded with substantial gifts.")]

#zh(id: "S010")[#text("圣所的中心，是嵌在墙里的一只盒子或柜子。其中保存着许多符药与魔法药剂；任何当地人都不相信，缺少这些东西还能够生活。这些制剂来自各种专门的从业者。其中最有力量的是巫医，必须以丰厚的礼物回报他们的帮助。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S011")[#text("However, the medicine men do not provide the curative potions for their clients, but decide what the ingredients should be and then write them down in an ancient and secret language. This writing is understood only by the medicine men and by the herbalists who, for another gift, provide the required charm.")]

#zh(id: "S011")[#text("不过，巫医并不直接向求助者提供治病的药剂，而是决定应当采用什么成分，然后用一种古老而秘密的语言写下来。只有巫医和草药师能够读懂这种文字；草药师收取另一份礼物之后，便提供所需的符药。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S012")[#text("The charm is not disposed of after it has served its purpose, but is placed in the charmbox of the household shrine. As these magical materials are specific for certain ills, and the real or imagined maladies of the people are many, the charm-box is usually full to overflowing. The magical packets are so numerous that people forget what their purposes were and fear to use them again.")]

#zh(id: "S012")[#text("符药完成用途之后，并不会被丢弃，而是放入家中圣所的符药箱。由于这些魔法材料各自针对特定病症，而人们真实或想象中的疾病又很多，符药箱通常塞得满满的。药包数量如此之多，以至于人们忘记了它们各有什么用途，又害怕重新使用。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S013")[#text("While the natives are very vague on this point, we can only assume that the idea in retaining all the old magical materials is that their presence in the charm-box, before which the body rituals are conducted, will in some way protect the worshiper.")]

#zh(id: "S013")[#text("虽然当地人对这一点说得十分含糊，我们只能推想：他们保留所有旧魔法材料，是因为相信这些材料留在举行身体仪式时面对的符药箱中，会以某种方式保护礼拜者。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S014")[#text("Beneath the charm-box is a small font. Each day every member of the family, in succession, enters the shrine room, bows his head before the charm-box, mingles different sorts of holy water in the font, and proceeds with a brief rite of ablution. The holy waters are secured from the Water Temple of the community, where the priests conduct elaborate ceremonies to make the liquid ritually pure.")]

#zh(id: "S014")[#text("符药箱下方有一个小水钵。每天，家中每个人依次进入圣所房间，在符药箱前低头，把不同种类的圣水混合在水钵中，然后进行一段简短的净身仪式。圣水取自社群的水神庙，那里的祭司举行繁复的典礼，使液体在仪式意义上变得纯洁。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S015")[#text("In the hierarchy of magical practitioners, and below the medicine men in prestige, are specialists whose designation is best translated as \"holy-mouth-men.\" The Nacirema have an almost pathological horror of and fascination with the mouth, the condition of which is believed to have a supernatural influence on all social relationships.")]

#zh(id: "S015")[#text("在巫术从业者的等级体系中，有一类声望低于巫医的专家；他们的称号，最适合译为“圣口者”。纳西雷马人对嘴有着近乎病态的恐惧与迷恋，相信嘴的状况会以超自然方式影响一切社会关系。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S016")[#text("Were it not for the rituals of the mouth, they believe that their teeth would fall out, their gums bleed, their jaws shrink, their friends desert them, and their lovers reject them. They also believe that a strong relationship exists between oral and moral characteristics. For example, there is a ritual ablution of the mouth for children which is supposed to improve their moral fiber.")]

#zh(id: "S016")[#text("他们相信，如果没有口腔仪式，牙齿便会脱落，牙龈会出血，下颌会萎缩，朋友会离去，恋人会拒绝自己。他们还相信，口腔的特征与道德品质之间有很强的关联。例如，有一种针对儿童的洗口仪式，据说可以改善他们的道德品格。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S017")[#text("The daily body ritual performed by everyone includes a mouth-rite. Despite the fact that these people are so punctilious about care of the mouth, this rite involves a practice which strikes the uninitiated stranger as revolting. It was reported to me that the ritual consists of inserting a small bundle of hog hairs into the mouth, along with certain magical powders, and then moving the bundle in a highly formalized series of gestures.")]

#zh(id: "S017")[#text("每个人每天的身体仪式，都包括一项口腔仪式。尽管这些人对照顾嘴如此一丝不苟，这项仪式中的一种做法，却会使不知内情的外来者感到恶心。有人向我报告，这种仪式是把一小束猪毛连同某种魔法粉末放进嘴里，再按照一套高度程式化的动作移动这束猪毛。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S018")[#text("In addition to the private mouth-rite, the people seek out a holy-mouth-man once or twice a year. These practitioners have an impressive set of paraphernalia, consisting of a variety of augers, awls, probes, and prods. The use of these items in the exorcism of the evils of the mouth involves almost unbelievable ritual torture of the client. The holy-mouth-man opens the client's mouth and, using the above mentioned tools, enlarges any holes which decay may have created in the teeth.")]

#zh(id: "S018")[#text("除了私下的口腔仪式，人们每年还会找圣口者一两次。这些从业者有一套令人印象深刻的器具，包括各种钻具、锥子、探针与刺具。用这些东西驱除口腔中的邪祟，会让求助者遭受几乎难以置信的仪式性折磨。圣口者打开求助者的嘴，使用上述工具，把牙齿因腐烂而形成的洞扩大。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S019")[#text("Magical materials are put into these holes. If there are no naturally occurring holes in the teeth, large sections of one or more teeth are gouged out so that the supernatural substance can be applied. In the client's view, the purpose of these ministrations is to arrest decay and to draw friends. The extremely sacred and traditional character of the rite is evident in the fact that the natives return to the holy-mouth-men year after year, despite the fact that their teeth continue to decay.")]

#zh(id: "S019")[#text("魔法材料被放入这些洞里。如果牙齿没有自然形成的洞，就会挖去一颗或几颗牙齿的大块部分，以便施加超自然物质。在求助者看来，这些服务是为了阻止腐烂，并吸引朋友。这项仪式极其神圣而传统的性质，从下面这个事实就可以看出：尽管牙齿继续腐烂，当地人仍年复一年地回到圣口者那里。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S020")[#text("It is to be hoped that, when a thorough study of the Nacirema is made, there will be careful inquiry into the personality structure of these people. One has but to watch the gleam in the eye of a holy-mouth-man, as he jabs an awl into an exposed nerve, to suspect that a certain amount of sadism is involved. If this can be established, a very interesting pattern emerges, for most of the population shows definite masochistic tendencies.")]

#zh(id: "S020")[#text("希望在对纳西雷马人进行全面研究时，人们会认真考察他们的人格结构。只要看一看圣口者把锥子刺入裸露神经时眼中闪动的光，就足以令人怀疑其中有某种程度的施虐倾向。如果这一点能得到证实，就会呈现出一种很有意思的模式，因为大部分居民表现出明显的受虐倾向。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S021")[#text("It was to these that Professor Linton referred in discussing a distinctive part of the daily body ritual which is performed only by men. This part of the rite includes scraping and lacerating the surface of the face with a sharp instrument. Special women's rites are performed only four times during each lunar month, but what they lack in frequency is made up in barbarity. As part of this ceremony, women bake their heads in small ovens for about an hour.")]

#zh(id: "S021")[#text("林顿教授谈到日常身体仪式中一种只有男子参加的特殊部分时，指的正是这些倾向。这部分仪式包括用锋利的器具刮擦、割伤脸部表面。妇女的特殊仪式，每个阴历月只举行四次，但频率的不足，由残酷程度来弥补。在这种典礼中，妇女把头放进小烤炉里烘烤约一小时。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S022")[#text("The theoretically interesting point is that what seems to be a preponderantly masochistic people have developed sadistic specialists.")]

#zh(id: "S022")[#text("在理论上有意思的一点是：一个看起来以受虐倾向为主的民族，却发展出了专门施虐的专家。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S023")[#text("The medicine men have an imposing temple, or latipso, in every community of any size. The more elaborate ceremonies required to treat very sick patients can only be performed at this temple. These ceremonies involve not only the thaumaturge but a permanent group of vestal maidens who move sedately about the temple chambers in distinctive costume and headdress.")]

#zh(id: "S023")[#text("在每一个有一定规模的社群中，巫医都拥有一座宏伟的神庙，称为 latipso。治疗重病患者所需的较复杂典礼，只能在这座神庙举行。这些典礼不仅需要施行奇术的巫医，也需要一群固定的贞洁侍女；她们穿着特殊服装、戴着特殊头饰，庄重地往来于神庙各室。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S024")[#text("The latipso ceremonies are so harsh that it is phenomenal that a fair proportion of the really sick natives who enter the temple ever recover. Small children whose indoctrination is still incomplete have been known to resist attempts to take them to the temple because \"that is where you go to die.\" Despite this fact, sick adults are not only willing but eager to undergo the protracted ritual purification, if they can afford to do so.")]

#zh(id: "S024")[#text("latipso 的典礼如此严酷，进入神庙的真正患病的当地人，竟有相当一部分能康复，实在令人惊讶。有些尚未完全接受教化的小孩，抗拒别人把他们带到神庙，因为“那是去死的地方”。尽管如此，患病的成年人不仅愿意，而且渴望接受漫长的仪式净化，只要他们负担得起。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S025")[#text("No matter how ill the supplicant or how grave the emergency, the guardians of many temples will not admit a client if he cannot give a rich gift to the custodian. Even after one has gained and survived the ceremonies, the guardians will not permit the neophyte to leave until he makes still another gift.")]

#zh(id: "S025")[#text("无论求助者病得多重，情况多么紧急，许多神庙的守卫都不会接纳一个无法向管理者献上丰厚礼物的人。即使已经进入并熬过了典礼，守卫也不会允许这位初入仪式者离开，直到他再献上一份礼物。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S026")[#text("The supplicant entering the temple is first stripped of all his or her clothes. In everyday life the Nacirema avoids exposure of his body and its natural functions. Bathing and excretory acts are performed only in the secrecy of the household shrine, where they are ritualized as part of the body-rites. Psychological shock results from the fact that body secrecy is suddenly lost upon entry into the latipso.")]

#zh(id: "S026")[#text("求助者一进入神庙，首先便被脱光所有衣服。在日常生活中，纳西雷马人避免暴露自己的身体及其自然机能。沐浴和排泄只能在家中圣所的隐秘环境中进行，并作为身体仪式的一部分加以仪式化。进入 latipso 后，身体的隐私突然消失，因此产生心理震动。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S027")[#text("A man, whose own wife has never seen him in an excretory act, suddenly finds himself naked and assisted by a vestal maiden while he performs his natural functions into a sacred vessel. This sort of ceremonial treatment is necessitated by the fact that the excreta are used by a diviner to ascertain the course and nature of the client's sickness. Female clients, on the other hand, find their naked bodies are subjected to the scrutiny, manipulation and prodding of the medicine men.")]

#zh(id: "S027")[#text("一个连妻子都从未见过自己排泄的男人，会突然发现自己赤裸着，在一位贞洁侍女的协助下，对着神圣的容器执行自然机能。这种仪式性处理之所以必要，是因为占卜者要用排泄物判断求助者疾病的发展与性质。另一方面，女性求助者则发现，自己的裸体受到巫医的查看、摆弄与戳探。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S028")[#text("Few supplicants in the temple are well enough to do anything but lie on their hard beds. The daily ceremonies, like the rites of the holy-mouth-men, involve discomfort and torture. With ritual precision, the vestals awaken their miserable charges each dawn and roll them about on their beds of pain while performing ablutions, in the formal movements of which the maidens are highly trained.")]

#zh(id: "S028")[#text("神庙中很少有求助者身体好到能够做躺在硬床上以外的事情。每日典礼与圣口者的仪式一样，包含不适与折磨。每逢黎明，侍女们便按照仪式精确地唤醒她们可怜的照顾对象，在这些痛苦的床上翻动他们，同时进行净身；侍女们接受过高度训练，能够以规定的动作完成这一过程。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S029")[#text("At other times they insert magic wands in the supplicant's mouth or force him to eat substances which are supposed to be healing. From time to time the medicine men come to their clients and jab magically treated needles into their flesh. The fact that these temple ceremonies may not cure, and may even kill the neophyte, in no way decreases the people's faith in the medicine men.")]

#zh(id: "S029")[#text("其他时候，她们会把魔杖插进求助者嘴里，或强迫他吃下据说有疗效的物质。巫医不时来到求助者身边，把经过魔法处理的针刺进他们的肉体。神庙典礼可能无法治好初入仪式者，甚至可能使他死亡，但这丝毫不会降低人们对巫医的信任。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S030")[#text("There remains one other kind of practitioner, known as a \"listener.\" This witchdoctor has the power to exorcise the devils that lodge in the heads of people who have been bewitched. The Nacirema believe that parents bewitch their own children. Mothers are particularly suspected of putting a curse on children while teaching them the secret body rituals. The counter-magic of the witchdoctor is unusual in its lack of ritual.")]

#zh(id: "S030")[#text("还有另一类从业者，称为“倾听者”。这位巫师能够驱除附在中了巫术的人头脑里的恶魔。纳西雷马人相信，父母会对自己的孩子施加巫术。尤其有人怀疑，母亲在教孩子秘密的身体仪式时，也给孩子下了诅咒。这位巫师的反巫术很特别，因为其中缺少仪式。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S031")[#text("The patient simply tells the \"listener\" all his troubles and fears, beginning with the earliest difficulties he can remember. The memory displayed by the Nacirema in these exorcism sessions is truly remarkable. It is not uncommon for the patient to bemoan the rejection he felt upon being weaned as a babe, and a few individuals even see their troubles going back to the traumatic effects of their own birth.")]

#zh(id: "S031")[#text("病人只需把所有烦恼与恐惧告诉“倾听者”，从自己能记起的最早困难说起。纳西雷马人在这些驱魔会谈中表现出的记忆，确实十分惊人。病人哀叹自己婴儿时期断奶时感到被拒绝的经历，并不罕见；少数人甚至把自己的烦恼追溯到出生本身造成的创伤性影响。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S032")[#text("In conclusion, mention must be made of certain practices which have their base in native esthetics but which depend upon the pervasive aversion to the natural body and its functions. There are ritual fasts to make fat people thin and ceremonial feasts to make thin people fat. Still other rites are used to make women's breasts larger if they are small, and smaller if they are large.")]

#zh(id: "S032")[#text("最后，必须提到某些以当地审美观为基础的做法；这些做法依赖于人们对自然身体及其机能的普遍厌恶。有仪式性禁食，使胖人变瘦，也有典礼性宴饮，使瘦人变胖。还有其他仪式，使小乳房变大，大乳房变小。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S033")[#text("General dissatisfaction with breast shape is symbolized in the fact that the ideal form is virtually outside the range of human variation. A few women afflicted with almost inhuman hyper-mammary development are so idolized that they make a handsome living by simply going from village to village and permitting the natives to stare at them for a fee.")]

#zh(id: "S033")[#text("对乳房形状的普遍不满，体现为理想形态几乎超出人类正常变异的范围。少数乳房发育达到近乎非人程度的妇女，受到如此偶像般的崇拜，以至于只需从一个村庄走到另一个村庄，让当地人付费观看，就能获得丰厚收入。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S034")[#text("Reference has already been made to the fact that excretory functions are ritualized, routinized, and relegated to secrecy. Natural reproductive functions are similarly distorted. Intercourse is taboo as a topic and scheduled as an act. Efforts are made to avoid pregnancy by the use of magical materials or by limiting intercourse to certain phases of the moon. Conception is actually very infrequent. When pregnant, women dress so as to hide their condition.")]

#zh(id: "S034")[#text("前面已经提到，排泄机能被仪式化、程序化，并被置于秘密之中。自然的生殖机能，也受到相似的扭曲。性交作为话题是禁忌，作为行为则按时安排。人们通过使用魔法材料，或者把性交限制在月亮的某些阶段，来努力避免怀孕。受孕实际上很少发生。妇女怀孕后，会穿衣掩盖自己的状况。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S035")[#text("Parturition takes place in secret, without friends or relatives to assist, and the majority of women do not nurse their infants.")]

#zh(id: "S035")[#text("分娩秘密进行，没有亲友协助；大多数妇女也不哺乳自己的婴儿。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S036")[#text("Our review of the ritual life of the Nacirema has certainly shown them to be a magic-ridden people. It is hard to understand how they have managed to exist so long under the burdens which they have imposed upon themselves. But even such exotic customs as these take on real meaning when they are viewed with the insight provided by Malinowski when he wrote:")]

#zh(id: "S036")[#text("我们对纳西雷马人仪式生活的考察，无疑表明他们是一个被巫术支配的民族。很难理解，他们在自己强加给自己的重重负担之下，怎么还能生存如此之久。不过，即使像这样的奇异习俗，借助马林诺夫斯基下面这段话所提供的洞见来观察，也会获得真正的意义：")]

#html.p(id: "en-S037")[#text("Looking from far and above, from our high places of safety in the developed civilization, it is easy to see all the crudity and irrelevance of magic. But without its power and guidance early man could not have mastered his practical difficulties as he has done, nor could man have advanced to the higher stages of civilization.")]

#zh(id: "S037")[#text("从远处、从高处，从我们身处发达文明的安全高地望去，很容易看出巫术的粗陋与不相干之处。然而，没有它的力量与指引，早期人类便不可能像已经做到的那样，克服实际困难；人类也不可能发展到更高的文明阶段。")]

